# Per-file counts of COMMENTS in api/test/**/*_test.exs that reproduce a
# bracketed list of two or more HTTP status literals (e.g. `[401, 403, 404]`).
# Such a comment is byte-identical to the assertion form it describes, so it
# answers every grep for the REMAINING work. Narrate it in prose instead.
# RATCHET: counts may only FALL. Regenerate with --baseline after fixing.
# Counts, NOT file:line — a line pin slides on any insertion above it.
# KEEP THIS FILE SHORT. A tripwire that grows stops discriminating; the
# eighth row is waved through by the seven above it. Fix the site instead.
# Paths are RELATIVE TO THE SCAN ROOT (api/test), not the repo root, so this
# same file is valid over a scratch copy — which is what lets --selftest arm
# (e) judge THIS baseline rather than a rewritten one.
